# .trivyignore
# Known upstream dependency vulnerabilities managed and triaged as of 2026-11-07.
# Resolved vulnerabilities from Spring Boot 3.4 / 4.0.0 baseline (Tomcat 10.1, Jackson 2.18/3.0, Spring Security 6.4/7.0.0,
# Spring Framework 6.2, Spring Data Commons 3.4, AssertJ 3.26) have been removed as they are resolved in Spring Boot 4.0.9.
# The remaining triaged CVEs below are either transitive dependencies in Google Cloud SDKs awaiting upstream release,
# not exploitable in this REST API service, or isolated to build-time Kotlin compiler configurations.
# Any NEW vulnerability beyond these triaged CVEs will fail the build (exit-code: 1).

# [HIGH] grpc-netty-shaded:1.70.0 - Netty MadeYouReset HTTP/2 DDoS Vulnerability
# Transitive via Google Cloud Spanner and Pub/Sub SDKs; upstream patch pending in Google Cloud Java client BOM.
CVE-2025-55163

# [HIGH] guava:33.4.0-jre - Denial of Service via unthrottled memory allocation during deserialization
# Transitive via Google Cloud SDK; application is a REST API and does not perform Java native deserialization of untrusted Guava objects.
CVE-2026-102554

# [HIGH] bcpg-jdk18on:1.80 - BC-JAVA: unbounded PGP AEAD chunk size leads to pre-auth resource exhaustion
# Isolated to build-time kotlinBouncyCastleConfiguration only; not present in runtime classpath or production artifacts.
CVE-2026-3505

# [CRITICAL] bcprov-jdk18on:1.80.2 - Bouncy Castle Name Constraints bypass via trailing dot
# Isolated to build-time kotlinBouncyCastleConfiguration only; not present in runtime classpath or production artifacts.
CVE-2026-8763

# [HIGH] bcprov-jdk18on:1.80.2 - Bouncy Castle Denial of Service via lazy ASN.1 sequence
# Isolated to build-time kotlinBouncyCastleConfiguration only; not present in runtime classpath or production artifacts.
CVE-2026-13506
